content.content:
Log format for every component: `timestamp level component event key=value`. `timestamp` is µs since the Unix epoch, written as an integer (the same unit as the on-disk record, so log lines and records can be joined), and `level` is one of `DEBUG`, `INFO`, `WARN` or `ERROR`. Every component builds its lines with the shared `gt_log_format` (`src/gt_log.c`) and writes them to stderr; children inherit the supervisor's stderr, so under systemd every line reaches the journal. Rule: whichever component refuses a reading records the gap (start, end, count), so no reading is ever lost silently. Besides the events in the table, storage logs `storage_start` / `storage_stop` (with segment, last `seq`, committed and refused counts), `segment_rollover`, and `hub_connected` / `hub_disconnected` / `hub_duplicate_client` for its one hub connection; `storage_degraded` carries `reason=write_failed` or `reason=queue_full`. The flag-to-name table is `src/storage_event.c`. Likewise the hub logs `hub_start`, `hub_stop` (with `sent`, the range `first_seq`..`last_seq` it sent, which `log_verify --sent` takes, `refused`, and `dropped` for records still queued at exit), `seq_resume` (with the `next_seq` it resumed at), and `sensor_connected` / `sensor_disconnected` / `sensor_refused` (`reason=too_many`) for its sensor connections; its flag-to-name tables are in `src/hub.c` and `src/hub_sender.c`.

| Component | Failure | Detection | Response | Log |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| Sensor (I2C) | Read fails (NACK, EIO, unplugged) | `read`/`ioctl` returns -1 | Retry 3× at 10 ms, then skip the sample; after 10 consecutive failures, mark offline and retry every 5 s | `i2c_read_error`, `sensor_offline`, `sensor_online` |
